    "job_description": "Role\r\nAI/ML Engineer Intern — Intelligent Recruiting & NLP\r\nCompany\r\nFictional test company: TalentFlow AI\r\nAbout the role\r\n• Build and evaluate AI/ML components for an intelligent recruitment platform that parses resumes, compares\r\ncandidates against job descriptions, ranks applicants, and generates recruiter-friendly explanations.\r\n• Work with Python and common machine-learning libraries to preprocess data, build evaluation pipelines, and\r\nintegrate NLP/LLM capabilities.\r\nResponsibilities\r\n• Develop Python services and data-processing pipelines for resume and job-description analysis.\r\n• Apply NLP techniques for text extraction, similarity matching, information retrieval, and candidate ranking.\r\n• Build and evaluate machine-learning models using appropriate metrics.\r\n• Work with embeddings, vector search, or retrieval-augmented generation where useful.\r\n• Create APIs or interactive prototypes for AI-powered recruiting workflows.\r\n• Clean, analyze, and visualize datasets; document experiments and findings.\r\n• Collaborate with engineers to test, debug, and improve AI features.\r\nRequired qualifications\r\n• Currently pursuing a degree in Computer Science, Artificial Intelligence, Data Science, or a related field.\r\n• Strong Python programming skills.\r\n• Hands-on understanding of Machine Learning and model evaluation.\r\n• Experience with Pandas, NumPy, and Scikit-learn.\r\n• Basic-to-intermediate NLP knowledge.\r\n• Understanding of embeddings, semantic similarity, or information retrieval.\r\n• Familiarity with Git/GitHub and building or consuming APIs.\r\nPreferred qualifications\r\n• Experience with LLMs, Generative AI, RAG, vector databases/vector search, or transformers.\r\n• Experience with PyTorch or another deep-learning framework.\r\n• Experience building Streamlit, FastAPI, or similar AI applications.\r\n• SQL/database experience.\r\n• Internship or project experience involving real-world AI/ML systems.\r\nScreening criteria\r\n• Python and ML fundamentals are the highest-priority requirements.\r\n• NLP/LLM and retrieval experience are strong differentiators.\r\n• Projects should demonstrate practical implementation, not only coursework.\r\n• Candidates with unrelated experience but weak Python/ML/NLP overlap should rank lo",
